{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1098315-torg-crossover-defining-the-cofd-s-world-laws","id":1098315,"title":"Torg Crossover: Defining the CofD's World Laws","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-29T19:17:39-07:00","id":1098315,"title":"Torg Crossover: Defining the CofD's World Laws","content":"In honor of the Torg Returns Kickstarter, I decided to think of ways to make the CofD a cosm.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor those of you who don't know, Torg is basically a setting + game system where various RPG settings (cosms) are attempting to invade and overtake Earth, at the behest of powerful villains called the High Lords who want the planet's &quot;possibility energy&quot; so they can one day rule the multiverse.<br /> <br /> \u200bThing is, along with the physical laws that enable them to work, each cosm has &quot;World Law&quot; that define its <i>narrative </i>\u200blaws. The pulpy Nile Empire rewards overly dramatic escapades, the cyberpunk Pan-Pacifica (Nippon Tech in the original Torg) gives you major buffs when seeking revenge. The CofD has a few that underpin the setting, so I'm figuring out what those are.<br /> <br /> \u200bOff the top of my head:<br /> <br /> The Law of Subtlety: <i>\u200bCunning, research, and spycraft overcome brute power and honor, almost every time</i>\u200b. All monsters have banes and bans on their behaviors that a perceptive and cautious researcher can intuit, all organizations have flaws that will damage them if struck precisely, the victor is the best ambusher. You don't get ahead in the Shadowed Realm without a good head on your shoulders. On the one hand, this does mean traditional heroes are likely doomed to be slapped down by people who don't mind hiding a knife or three up their sleeves, but it also means nobody, not even the High Lords themselves, cannot be brought down or hurt-all even the weakest, lowliest mortal needs to have is the proper intel and the will to carry out their schemes.<br /> <br /> The Law Of Occult Mystery: <i>\u200bSeek the supernatural, and ye shall find-as it finds you.</i>\u200b People in the Shadowed Realm are not stupid-they know damn well ghosts exist, the wolves that howl sometimes walk as men, that there seems to be more than simple privilege that keeps the rich rich, and the poor poor. They just happen to know this Law on an intuitive level; if someone looks for the occult underpinning of the world, she will at least get a general idea of the forces behind whatever she's looking at-and invariably, if said &quot;whatever&quot; doesn't catch on through luck, intuition, or simple paranoia, some other supernatural force will. If you dare to scratch the surface, be prepared to join whatever you find for the long haul.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Law of Desire and Exchange: <i>\u200bAll power, all goals have a price-and if you are willing to pay, those power and goals can be anything.</i>\u200b This is both warning and promise. Everyone in the Shadowed Realm can become a monster, should fate, another, or they themselves chose it. All monsters have needs and weaknesses that torment them and the world around them-but they also get <i>\u200bpower, </i>\u200band power gives them agency, the ability to change the world around them for the better or worse. Anything in the world, even bringing back the dead, is possible with enough effort and the right payment-the trouble is whether you were ripped off, or if you'll be able to live with yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T21:05:32-07:00","id":1098341,"title":"","content":"This is probably not so much a separate Law as a derived middle ground between the Law of Subtlety and the Law of Occult Mystery, but\u2026<br /> <br /> The Law of Conspiracy: <i>Naked monstrosity sows the seeds of its own destruction - mortal cover and like-minded monsters stave off ruin equally well or better than raw power alone.</i> A recurrent aspect of the Shadowed Realm is that monsters who bear a strong resemblance to the creatures of mortal folklore tend to have little better recourse; the integrated societies of witches and werewolves and vampires are better-equipped and less desperate thanks to their ability to divide the strain of their activities among a larger group and a wider segment of human society. Proxies narrowly beat out hunting grounds in value for all but the most antisocial monsters \u2014 and the most antisocial monsters soon develop a reputation that calls for their removal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T23:49:13-07:00","id":1098361,"title":"","content":"Another extrapolation from the above three laws, this time from the Law of Desire and Exchange;<br /> <br /> The Law of Inverse Correlation between Power and Humanity: <i>The heights of supernatural potency in any form are accompanied by an increasing detachment from the human condition and mindse</i>t. All monsters have the potential to expand their supernatural capabilities, even potentially achieving what is functionally godhood with the right vehicle and direction. This however estranges the monsters further from humanity, be it their own human origins or their ability to interact with humans, likely both. The reverse is true, meaning that actions which require the monster to abandon their humanity often reward it with supernatural power. Another aspect of this Law is that some beings may return to a semblance of humanity by sacrificing their monstrous power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T15:22:28-07:00","id":1098579,"title":"","content":"Excellent colloraries. <br /> <br /> Though, now I'm wondering what and who the High Lord is...if there is even a distinct one. It fits if there are multiple contenders fighting over the Darkness Device (the eldrtich machines that give High Lords their powers) who will occasionally call truces to manifest their dimension-altering abilities. Perhaps the Celestial Flange is called that because it can make &quot;pipes&quot; to other worlds? <br /> <br /> The first couple contenders that come to my mind are the Dark Mother and the collective consciousness of the Exarchs-savage nature vs corrupt civilization. Of course, the real reason nobody has claimed the Flange is that it obeys the World Laws too, and no side really wants to pay its asking price (the Mother would have to give up her love for her children, the Exarchs their immortality).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T16:58:02-07:00","id":1098614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1098315-torg-crossover-defining-the-cofd-s-world-laws?p=1098579#post1098579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excellent colloraries.<br /> <br /> Though, now I'm wondering what and who the High Lord is...if there is even a distinct one. It fits if there are multiple contenders fighting over the Darkness Device (the eldrtich machines that give High Lords their powers) who will occasionally call truces to manifest their dimension-altering abilities. Perhaps the Celestial Flange is called that because it can make &quot;pipes&quot; to other worlds?<br /> <br /> The first couple contenders that come to my mind are the Dark Mother and the collective consciousness of the Exarchs-savage nature vs corrupt civilization. Of course, the real reason nobody has claimed the Flange is that it obeys the World Laws too, and no side really wants to pay its asking price (the Mother would have to give up her love for her children, the Exarchs their immortality).</div> </div> </div> </div>And the God-Machine either is it, or is busily trying to hack it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T18:56:27-07:00","id":1098635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1098315-torg-crossover-defining-the-cofd-s-world-laws?p=1098614#post1098614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And the God-Machine either is it, or is busily trying to hack it?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAnswer Hazy, Try Again At Own Table.<br /> <br /> \u200bI will say the third major faction I have in mind is a powerful Unchained lord who keeps it vague if he's trying to win the Flange for his own reasons, for a war against the Machine, or to transfer ownership over to it so as to bring its clockwork perfection to the multiverse. None conflicts with the Flange being the core of the Machine itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}